    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "What's confusing here is that since the Helper is a dependency, we flag it as a \"chore\", but if the state management was directly in InstantSearch, we would have flagged it as a \"fix\".\r\n\r\nThis is why I think we shouldn't care about it being a \"chore\", it's a \"fix\" for the users.\r\n\r\nI recommend being explicit about the bug fix in the changelog.\r\n\r\nWdyt?\r\n\r\n```suggestion\r\n\r\nThis version fixes a case where refinements for a facet with a name that matches a substring of another facet could be cleared by mistake. The fix was addressed in the [helper of the library](https://github.com/algolia/algoliasearch-helper-js/pull/760).\r\n```",
